§5 ⚜ ᴀ ꜱᴛᴏʀʏ ꜱᴇʀɪᴇꜱ ⚜
#- §5╔═.✵.════════╗   §2ʙᴇ ᴍᴇʀʀʏ ᴀɴᴅ ꜰʀɪɢʜᴛ
§5╚════════.✵.═╝
§8“§2My mother told me you would find me§8,” said the young girl withering from the harsh winter breeze. “§5Only if you didn’t find me first little one§8” replies the ominous hooded figure sheltering behind a tree trunk. 
#- §8Their voice is obscure and almost sounds like they are glitching in and out. “§5You’ll catch your death of cold if you linger here any longer§8”. The girl forces herself upright, making sure her recently obtained sword is close by. “§2Are you here to hurt me§8?” she whispers as she places a hand
#- §8upon the hilt of the sword. The hooded figure calmly walks out from behind the safety of the trees and steps into full view without a word in return. The girl still can’t focus clearly on them. She questions if her winter weakness is to blame or if the strange figure is intentionally making
#- §8this happen. “§2So what now, are you just going to stand there watching me§8?” The figure moves forward a few steps, leaving deep footprints in the carpet of snow. The girl holds up the sword with trembling hands, signalling them to go no further. They keep moving forwards... 
#- §8The girl stands her ground, until the point of the blade digs slightly into the chest of the figure. “§5If I was here for that, I would have done so by now§8”. The girl is growing fast but small, the figure is more adult in size, towering above her. All she can see under the hood is a shadowy face with
#- §8piercing white eyes. Distorted like looking through dark crystals. Despite this, she has no doubt that this person had to be §5ɨȶ§8, the one she was warned about. “§5The time for fighting shall come Fern, but for now I’m here to give my thanks little one§8.” 
A gloved hand slides the blade away. 
#- §8Confused and afraid the girl tries to keep eye contact. “§5I truly believed that I’d met my match this time around, and then like a shining star you set me free§8”. The fear turns into anger as the girl shouts 
“§2BY MISTAKE§8!” 
The figure let’s out a 'half-laugh-half-sigh' as they kneel down to
#- §8position themselves more face to face. “§5They always do little one, in the end§8”. They lift the cloak and reveal something wrapped in purple silk. “§5Here little one, call this a 'special' Christmas present from me to you§8”. 
The girls first thought was how they could hide that under there,
#- §8but then quickly snapped back into defensive mode. “§2That’s a trap, do you really think I would fall for this§8?”. A purple hue of light begins to sparkle around the gift and the silk slowly disintegrates up in the air. A wooden box is left behind with a spyglass carved on 
#- §8the top. “§2The Order Of The Spyglass§8?” the girl says under her breath. “§5Not quite...§8” replies the figure merrily and with a hint of excitement. The box bursts open before the girl could blink. Flustered but forever curious she takes a look at the contents. Inside is a pile of strange books!
#- §8“§2Books, what am I meant to do with these, and why do they look so… weird§8?” 

The figure leaves the box on the ground before standing again and slowly backing away. 

“§5Where I come from, we like calling them…
§dWitch-Craft Magazine§8.”
#- §8More purple light starts to form underneath the figure's cloak and hood. “§5I think you’ll find these to be a very interesting read§8.” The girl picks up the first book on the pile and flips to the first page. 

“§2Who is Sweetpea§8?”
#- §8With that, the figure vanishes with a giant explosion of magical light. Snow begins to fall as the sparkling lights shine so beautifully. Creating a mixture of §5purple§8, §6gold§8 and §2green§8 against every snowflake. The girl holds the book tightly watching in amazement as the once-empty
#- §8forest clearing starts blooming with life. Snowdrops sprout, vines twist, and water flows. The trees start singing along with the winter wind. The girl spots a wild stag standing nearby. The antlers are full of §6sweetpea§8 petals and§2 fern§8 leaves. She reaches out towards the stag before it
#- §8quickly fades away. And then everything went quiet like none of this ever happened... 

