§9 A guide for making a        house a home!
#-    §9⛏*⋆§1Article Six§9⋆*⛏
       §4ᴰᵒ ʸᵒᵘ ʷᵃⁿᵗ ᵗᵒ 
     ᵇᵘⁱˡᵈ ᵃ ˢⁿᵒʷ ᵍᵒˡᵉᵐ?   
§8-------------------
§1Okay, I don't 'do' this whole Christmas thing but I have some building ideas for you!

§b❄§11. Lazy Snow!
Do you want to have lots of snow on the floor but are lazy, well here is a simple
#- §1way of making snow and getting it everywhere; Snow Golems! Just build yourself a little (§3or big§1) army of these dudes by placing two snow blocks upright and plonking a carved pumpkin on top and BOOOM! These creepy things will not only help protect you from hostile mobs but will
#- §1also leave snow behind them... job done! If they stay alive they are also kind of cool (§3pun intended§1), but beware, rain will unalive them, the poor things. You can also remove the 'creepy' (§3don't know why anyone would§1) by sheering the pumpkin head right off, then you got a snowman!
#- §b❄§12. You can go above and beyond for an xmas tree but try these cool ideas (§3yes I made the same pun again§1): You can use different types of leaves so it looks cooler (§3I did it again§1). If you have some xmas heads like little gifts or even balls they look cool (§3deal with it§1). If not heads, 
#- §1try item frames with wool in them. Glowing frames can make it look (§3you guessed it§1) cooler. Candles also kinda work but are a bit of a fire safety hazard... 

§b❄§13. Want an xmas star on top? Make the tree big enouth where you have a single block left at the top and try
#- §1placing a amethyst block on there with some amethyst crystals on the block... that one actually does look very §3COOL§1. You can also do the same thing with glass (§3one block with panes on it, just has no light, not as cool§1). An end rod sticking out can also do the trick. §3Cool!
#- §8-------------------
§9⛏§1I’ll try to be more enthusiastic in the next Crafty Witches!§9⛏
