§5 ⚜ ᴀ ꜱᴛᴏʀʏ ꜱᴇʀɪᴇꜱ ⚜
#- §5╔═.✵.════════╗  §2       ᴛʜᴇ ᴍᴀɢɪᴄ 
     ᴏꜰ ᴄʜʀɪꜱᴛᴍᴀꜱ!
§5╚════════.✵.═╝
§2Sweetpea is a kind and gentle soul who used to love nothing more than to spend her days exploring the enchanted woods that surrounded her home. Suddenly finding herself back there, she takes a moment
#- §2to enjoy the beauty of the snow-covered trees. As she wanders deeper into the forest, she stumbles upon a small clearing. She carefully watches from the shadows as an ominous hooded figure approaches a young girl. She looks on as the story she read not that long ago plays out before
#- §2her eyes. A little bit frozen in fear to intervene. As the hooded figure disappears into the snow, the girl opens her new collection of books and begins to read each one. Sweetpea can sense the magic in the words, and the impact they have on this young mind full of destiny. 
#- §2Not knowing how long she has, Sweetpea steps out of the shadows and shows herself to the girl... 

"§6Hello there§2," 
the shy witch says, approaching the girl. 

"§6My name is 
Sweetpea. What are you reading§2?"
#- §2The girl looks up, her eyes bright and curious. "These are your books," holding up a volume with a familiar cover. "I love reading your stories. They make me 
feel so... alive." 

Sweetpea nodded, feeling a surge of pride. "§6Thank you§2," Sweetpea says, smiling.
#- §2"§6I'm glad you enjoy my stories. They mean a lot to me… and Craftadia I guess§2." 
The girl's eyes are shining. "I know," she says. "I can feel the magic in your words. It's like you're casting a spell on me when I read them." Sweetpea chuckles. "§6That's a very sweet way of putting it§2." she replies.
#- §2"§6I also believe in the power of books. They can transport us to different worlds and introduce us to 
new ideas and experiences... 
They can change our lives in ways we never thought possible§2." Sweetpea smiles, feeling a warm glow in her heart. She is glad to have shared
#- §2this impossible moment with Fern. “I agree,” said the girl. “The power of books is something that can never be taken away from us. They can inspire us, teach us, and help us to connect with others who share our passions. And that is the greatest magic of all." Sweetpea couldn't
#- §2help but tear up. "§6Well, I'm glad we had this chat§2," Sweetpea says, standing up. "§6But I'm afraid I have to be on my way. I need to find my way back home… wherever that is§2." The girl nods, standing up as well. "Of course, disappear back to your timeline, where you belong, and deal with §5ɨȶ§2 for me!"
#- §2she says with a smirk on her face. Snow and the aftermath of magic still fill the air.
Sweetpea finally starts to understand the place where she truly belongs... 
§l
Sweetpea has found a home in the pages of her own books.
#- §2Sprouting from under her feet, bright blossoms begin climbing around her. Knowing there is not much time left, and yet, all the time in the world, a feeling of warmth wraps around her. She knows now is her chance to say something that could shape the destiny of this young flower...
#- §2"§6Before I go, remember this; blossom may be short-lived but its beauty and fragrance linger long after they have fallen... don't be scared of falling! Don't be scared 
of §0The Darkness§6! 
And.... and....§2"

§6"§oBe genuine like fern 
in the forest...§0§6" 
#- §2With that, the blossoms consume Sweetpea and quickly fade away. Everything goes quiet once again, like this never happened...
